1
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:24,240
Anyone without money, come to my place.

2
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:28,940
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:36,020
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:36,420
Me

5
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,680
Somehow or other, it'll all work out.

6
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:47,100
Fuwahahahahahahahaha!

7
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

8
00:01:00,790 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:11,900
Look, it's burning, Akaneru too.

10
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:18,240
Somehow or other, it'll all work out.

11
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,480
You understand, right?
Understood, understood.

12
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,400
Once you understand,
keep quiet and follow me.

13
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:43,280
Crossroads of Fate

14
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:50,520
Trouble has arisen in your work.

15
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,360
What will you do?

16
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:54,320
A: Leave it to a colleague

17
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,480
B: Solve it yourself

18
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,240
A

19
00:01:57,980 --> 00:01:58,560
So, A.

20
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:01,100
Just then, your boss happened to show up.

21
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:02,120
What will you do?

22
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,100
A: Make an excuse

23
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,240
B: Run away

24
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,800
This is a tough one, but I'll go with B.

25
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,560
B, then. Your fortune for today is...

26
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:14,420
the worst day ever.

27
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:17,160
Nothing you do will go well.

28
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,280
Again with this?

29
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:21,140
That's five times in a row now.

30
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:23,780
That one doesn't count, I'm redoing it.

31
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:26,120
Enough already!

32
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,620
Senpai

33
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,280
Honda-san.

34
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,400
Welcome.

35
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,700
What are you doing?

36
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:33,840
Look at this.

37
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,600
It's a fortune-telling thing
that came with a magazine.

38
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,440
See, it's laid out as a flowchart.

39
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:42,200
The one where you keep picking A or B

40
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:47,320
Ryo-san's been getting nothing but the worst day since earlier,
so he keeps restarting it.

41
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:50,780
Shut up, you didn't get a
good result either, did you?

42
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:53,680
Was it the "perfectly ordinary day" one?

43
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:56,340
Yeah, ordinary is good enough for me.

44
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,880
You have no ambition at all.

45
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:01,180
That's not the point, is it?

46
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:04,340
Terai-san, it's time for patrol.

47
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:07,780
Right, I'm off then. Take care of things.

48
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:09,540
Take care!

49
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:11,040
Be careful.

50
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,560
Right, let's continue, Reiko.

51
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,540
What, are we still doing this?

52
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:19,540
Of course. We'll keep doing it as many
times as it takes to get a good result.

53
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:22,280
Wait a moment.

54
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,780
Hello, Kameari Park police box.

55
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,680
Chief Ohara.

56
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:29,120
What, a bank robbery?

57
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:33,090
Understood, Ryo-chan.

58
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:35,800
Apparently,
a robber broke into Suchara Bank.

59
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,100
Head to the scene right away!

60
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,640
Got it!

61
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:40,500
It's the god.

62
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,920
Dame-Taro and Honoonosuke.

63
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:44,220
Long time no see.

64
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:47,740
You still haven't been fired,
you delinquent cop?

65
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:48,680
Shut up.

66
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,880
Where are you going, god?

67
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:52,720
Yeah, an incident has come up.

68
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,860
I'm just heading over to Suchara Bank now.

69
00:03:56,900 --> 00:04:01,480
Wait, my fortune today is the worst.
If I go to the scene like this,

70
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:03,940
get a car ready.

71
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,760
Wait, suspects, arrest them!

72
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,180
Shut up!

73
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:18,540
Maybe it's better to leave this to Dame
Taro and the others instead of going myself.

74
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:19,540
What's wrong?

75
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,220
Alright, I've decided.

76
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:24,560
I'm leaving this case to you.

77
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:26,480
Senpai!

78
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:28,883
If you work hard and get results,

79
00:04:28,933 --> 00:04:32,600
they might even build
you a robot police station!

80
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,880
A robot police station!?

81
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:38,240
Heh! I'm fired up now!

82
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:39,880
Let's go, Dame Taro!

83
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,180
Wait, hold on a second!

84
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,680
Is that really okay, senpai?

85
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:46,731
Don't mind it!
On days with bad luck like this,

86
00:04:46,781 --> 00:04:49,200
it's better not to do any work at all!

87
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:52,420
So you don't want to work that badly?!

88
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:53,720
Going or not!

89
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,820
I told you to head straight to the scene,

90
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,120
and I had Reiko pass that message along to you,
didn't I?

91
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,280
Uh-oh, what do I do?

92
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,860
Make up a good excuse or run away?

93
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:08,780
Run away!

94
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,280
Ryotsu!

95
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:28,160
Well, this is oil, damn it.

96
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:31,080
Hey, you dropped your bag!

97
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:33,500
Get back here!

98
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:39,220
You, bank robber, you're under arrest!

99
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:40,140
What?

100
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,000
Come quietly and take your restraints!

101
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,160
It's me, look closely, you idiot!

102
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,780
What, an idiot?

103
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:55,020
Oh no, when this guy gets angry,

104
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,640
That might be...

105
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,760
Sure enough.

106
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:19,500
Today really is the worst day.

107
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,140
Wait a moment.

108
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:26,040
No matter what, it ended way too quickly.

109
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,840
Yeah, running away from the
chief back there was the mistake.

110
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,000
Let's do it over.

111
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:46,600
Back.

112
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:50,000
What do you mean, back, Ryotsu?

113
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:57,400
I told Reiko to tell you to head straight to the scene,
didn't I?

114
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,060
Now, here's the problem.

115
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:05,300
Last time you chose option B,
run away, and it ended badly for you.

116
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:06,560
This time,

117
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:09,900
it's option A.

118
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:17,180
Actually, the hospital just called. Dad
was in an accident and has been admitted.

119
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:17,540
and...

120
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:21,620
Your dad's over there, perfectly fine.

121
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:25,000
Kankichi, I dropped my wallet.

122
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:27,460
I was in trouble and ran into Mr. Ohara.

123
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:29,640
He let me hitch a ride in the patrol car.

124
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,920
So why at a time like this...?

125
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:35,860
Sorry, I made a mistake.
It was Mom, not Dad.

126
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,620
What did you say about me?

127
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,880
Making lame excuses like that is unbecoming!

128
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:45,220
If you don't want to get fired,
get to the scene quickly!

129
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:46,920
No, but...

130
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,120
Hey, what kind of mic is this!

131
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:50,520
Thief!

132
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,080
Whoa!

133
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:54,080
Ryotsu, do something!

134
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,040
Stop!

135
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:57,620
Senpai!

136
00:07:58,140 --> 00:07:59,560
Stop right there!

137
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,200
Is that a robot soldier?

138
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,700
So, could that have been
the bank robber just now?

139
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:06,860
Get out of the way, you!

140
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,960
Kuwajū!

141
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:11,080
I'm not sticking to you on purpose either!

142
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:22,520
Aaaaaaah!

143
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:27,560
Ouch! Hey, this is a factory,
isn't it! Okay.

144
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:31,220
Give up, bank robber!

145
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:38,000
You're under arrest! If you come here,
things will get bad! What, you idiot?

146
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:42,260
Don't mock Rabat!

147
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:46,580
Stop it!

148
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:54,500
Just as I thought, today is the worst day.

149
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:58,900
Wait a minute!

150
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,640
This is even worse than before!

151
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:04,300
Right, meeting the Chief
was already game over.

152
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,340
We have to start over from way back.

153
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:28,440
I'm back.

154
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,820
No, it's nothing.

155
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,920
Where are you going, oh god?

156
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,740
Actually, an incident has occurred.

157
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:37,960
I was just about to head to Suchara Bank.

158
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:40,220
What's wrong?

159
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:45,520
If you choose A here,
you'll run into Chief Ohara after this,

160
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,980
and you'll meet a miserable end.

161
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,660
So, naturally,

162
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:52,400
it's B.

163
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:53,620
B?

164
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:58,340
Sorry, but I don't have
time to deal with you two.

165
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:59,700
Let's go, Honda!

166
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:00,800
Haah...

167
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:02,780
What kind of name is that?!

168
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,960
Let's go, Ryotsu-no-danna!

169
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:11,060
Heavens.

170
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,420
This should keep the worst from happening.

171
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,440
What do you mean by that, Ryo-san?

172
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:22,680
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

173
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:27,060
A new pachinko parlor

174
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:29,180
A: Stop by the pachinko parlor.

175
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,500
B: Head straight to the scene.

176
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,660
Alright, it's A.

177
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,820
Honda, stop!

178
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,860
Hey, weren't we supposed
to be going to Suchara Bank?

179
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:45,360
It's fine.
I've got no intention of working today.

180
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,740
Don't blame me if you get scolded later.

181
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:49,460
Yay!

182
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:57,540
Just as I thought, walking into this
pachinko parlor was the right call.

183
00:10:57,540 --> 00:11:00,180
Senpai,
shouldn't we think about stopping soon?

184
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:02,560
What are you talking about?
I'm on a winning streak here!

185
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,000
How could I quit now?

186
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:07,260
Attention, customers!
We have an announcement!

187
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:08,293
Today,

188
00:11:08,343 --> 00:11:12,200
we have a special limited-edition item
to commemorate our grand reopening!

189
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:16,120
And that is none other than
premium Japanese black beef!

190
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,820
Hey, real cows?! Let's go check it out!

191
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:30,960
Uh-oh, not good!

192
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:47,860
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

193
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:51,360
Based on the pattern so far,
if Honōnosuke catches me, I'm in for it!

194
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:54,820
Run! Run away from that stupid robot!

195
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,580
What? Stupid, did you say?

196
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,400
Don't you dare call robots stupid!

197
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:05,260
Chest!

198
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,960
Okay, I got past it.

199
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:17,958
Alright,

200
00:12:18,008 --> 00:12:22,760
preparations are complete.

201
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:25,100
Well then,
let's take a break until the rehearsal.

202
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:27,280
So cute! Dive in!

203
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:31,960
What!

204
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:41,100
Today really is the worst day ever!

205
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,460
No way!

206
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:47,360
This is no good at all!

207
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:50,020
We're starting over from the very beginning!

208
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:14,740
Yeah, well, I'm off then.

209
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:15,900
Take care of things.

210
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,700
Have a good one!

211
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:18,980
Be careful.

212
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:20,920
Hey, I'm back.

213
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,440
What are you talking about?

214
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:24,960
No, never mind.

215
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:27,880
Wait a second.

216
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,580
If I analyze the patterns so far,

217
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:33,840
whenever I pick the one I think is right,

218
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,660
a miserable ending awaits.

219
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,480
So that means

220
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:39,860
Ah ah ah ah

221
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:41,800
I should choose the opposite.

222
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:44,660
Choose the opposite.

223
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:47,560
Ryo-chan

224
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:50,060
I heard a robber broke into Suchaika Bank.

225
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,440
Head straight to the scene.

226
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,040
Got it.

227
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,080
Gods.

228
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,220
Honoo-no-Suke and Dame-Tarō

229
00:13:57,220 --> 00:14:00,300
Normally I'd leave this to
Dame-Tarō and the others,

230
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:02,540
but I'll grit my teeth and choose B here.

231
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:03,440
Sorry, but

232
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:05,700
I don't have time to deal with you lot.

233
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,900
Let's go, Honda!

234
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,040
A new pachinko parlor

235
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:17,060
Normally I'd stop by a pachinko parlor,

236
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,440
but I'll grit my teeth
here too and go with B.

237
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,080
Hey, Ryo-san.

238
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:31,780
Honda, what's up?

239
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,980
Did you just get a call from
your friends at the toy shop?

240
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:40,260
The limited-edition Ashigaru version figure from the CI Castle series
that you were looking for, Ryo-san,

241
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:45,700
is going on sale suddenly at an event venue,
only 100 sets.

242
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:46,780
What?

243
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:50,400
If we go now, we might just make it.

244
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,160
What do you want to do?

245
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:53,840
A, go buy it right away.

246
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:55,960
B, hold off here.

247
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:02,220
Come on, that's obvious. Of course,

248
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:07,840
if I honestly pick the picture here,
I'll fall into the same pattern as before

249
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:12,780
and I'm sure to meet
the same fate as always.

250
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:16,020
Damn it, damn it, it has to be B here!

251
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:16,400
B?

252
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:19,760
I'm on my way to work.

253
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:23,020
I don't have time for that. Hurry up, Honda!

254
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:24,080
Got it.

255
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:34,680
Damn it, the figure at the match venue...

256
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:37,660
What are you muttering about, Ryotsu?

257
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:39,060
Nothing.

258
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:41,480
Hey, Ryotsu.

259
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,720
What is it, Sagonji?

260
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,140
Perfect timing.

261
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:48,560
At the event venue in Ikebukuro,

262
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:53,720
the limited edition of Dokinemo
Fight Super Edition is going on sale.

263
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,660
What?

264
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:57,160
Of course you're coming too, right?

265
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:00,000
I'll go buy it right away.

266
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:01,980
I have to hold myself back here.

267
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:09,280
I'd love to go, but I can't
afford to be doing that right now.

268
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:14,240
Ryotsu.

269
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,680
Ryotsu, this is bad!

270
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:28,200
At the event venue in Asakusa, the Elephant
Lottery Car Perfect Model is going on sale!

271
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:44,660
Ryo-san,
I found that video you were looking for!

272
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:47,100
Ryo-san, look at this sake!

273
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:50,220
Ryo-san, I got tickets for K-1!

274
00:16:51,060 --> 00:16:53,060
Ryo-san,
let's go to the horse races together!

275
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:56,680
Ryo-san, here's the new genseng data!

276
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,780
Long time no see, Arakan-chan!

277
00:16:58,780 --> 00:16:59,600
Ryo-san!

278
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,760
No, no, no way!

279
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:06,120
I won't be fooled by those options!

280
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:08,620
I'm heading straight to the scene.

281
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,180
Finally arrived.

282
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:17,480
It's Ryotsu Kankichi.

283
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:22,360
Komachi, Naoko. Are you two the only ones here?
Where are the others?

284
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,020
They haven't come yet.

285
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:27,880
We happened to be patrolling nearby,
so we got here first.

286
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,800
Is the suspect still inside?

287
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,280
Yes.

288
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:33,280
But if we don't do something fast,
they'll get away.

289
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:35,340
What should we do?

290
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,940
A: Storm in right now.

291
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:40,620
B: Wait for backup.

292
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:42,880
Either one could work here.

293
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,140
If it were me, normally,

294
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:46,720
I'd want to wrap the job up quickly.

295
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:47,660
I'd choose A.

296
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:49,660
That means, conversely,

297
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,100
here it's B.

298
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:56,820
It's dangerous for us to push in alone.

299
00:17:56,820 --> 00:17:58,620
We wait for backup.

300
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,560
Got it.

301
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:03,180
They've come out.

302
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:06,240
They're going to scatter and run!

303
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:08,120
Right!

304
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,920
A, pursue the suspect who fled to the right.

305
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:14,520
B, pursue the suspect who fled to the left.

306
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:18,240
Doesn't matter which! It's A here!

307
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:19,040
A?

308
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:23,220
Honda and I will chase the
suspect who fled to the right!

309
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,900
You two go after the
one who fled to the left!

310
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:26,400
Got it!

311
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:37,000
All right! We've caught up!

312
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:52,480
Here at Kameari Stadium, an unprecedented first-ever
baseball tournament by construction workers is about to begin.

313
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:56,100
Now, the leadoff batter
steps up to the plate.

314
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:57,380
Play ball!

315
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:01,800
The power shovel on the mound
winds up and throws the first pitch.

316
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:03,100
It's thrown!

317
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,260
Here it comes!

318
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:08,560
It's hit!

319
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,840
A big one, a big one, soaring far and high!

320
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:12,780
Is it going in?

321
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,560
The center crane has caught it!

322
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:17,060
No, it bounced off!

323
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:17,500
Yes!

324
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:18,715
Now,

325
00:19:18,765 --> 00:19:22,540
the left fielder, the road roller, and the right fielder,
the bulldozer, are heading for the ball!

326
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:25,300
The bulldozer picks up the ball!

327
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:29,660
W-why does this have to happen to me...

328
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:33,820
Whoa! Here the dump truck
and the concrete mixer collide!

329
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:44,700
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

330
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:48,440
Eeeeeh, what a mess! What a terrible day!

331
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:55,060
If this keeps up, the concrete will harden!
Just a little more!

332
00:19:55,640 --> 00:20:00,220
Now it's time for the special entry, the Type 7 medium tank!
No, wait!

333
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:02,640
Eeeeeeh!

334
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:09,220
Today really is the worst day ever.

335
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:12,700
No, no, no.

336
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,960
I'll go with the left after all.

337
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:15,700
It's B.

338
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,700
They're going to scatter and run!

339
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:28,260
What do we do, senpai?

340
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,600
B!

341
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:29,960
B?

342
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:33,860
Honda and I will chase
the suspect who fled left.

343
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:36,340
You two go after the one who ran right.

344
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:37,160
Got it.

345
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:43,780
Stop, you bastard!

346
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:51,720
What the hell, you bastard?

347
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:55,560
Hey, stop it! Let go, you goddamn idiot!

348
00:20:56,880 --> 00:21:00,720
Here at Kameari Stadium, for the
first time ever, a baseball tournament

349
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:03,440
organized by construction
workers is about to begin.

350
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:05,160
Play ball!

351
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:09,500
The power shovel on the mound
winds up for the first pitch!

352
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:10,940
He throws it!

353
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:14,160
No way!

354
00:21:14,260 --> 00:21:14,880
Shovel!

355
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:16,300
Crane-ser!

356
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:17,180
It's hit!

357
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:19,320
Big, big!

358
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:20,220
It's soaring up there!

359
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:20,980
Is it going in?

360
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:22,080
Whoa!

361
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,320
The center fielder, the Placer!

362
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:23,800
He's got it!

363
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:25,180
No, it bounced off!

364
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:35,540
In the end,

365
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,840
same as before

366
00:21:40,470 --> 00:21:53,600
Today really is the worst day ever.

367
00:21:57,460 --> 00:21:59,140
So in the end, it comes down to this.

368
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:01,940
So we can't wait for backup, then.

369
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:06,180
Just do that. Okay, let's head back!

370
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:16,900
The suspect's still inside? A...
but if we don't act fast, they'll get away.

371
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:19,780
Right, A: we're charging in!

372
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:30,040
Where do we get in? A: front door,
B: back door, C: second-floor window.

373
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:32,800
Here, it's A. The front door!

374
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:33,600
Alright!

375
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:40,580
Damn, this one's no good?
Then on to the next!

376
00:22:41,980 --> 00:22:45,720
Ryo-san, where do we get in?

377
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:47,760
It's B. The back door!

378
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:48,400
Alright!

379
00:22:56,860 --> 00:22:59,200
Damn it,
why does it always end up like this?

380
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:01,480
Next! Choose C!

381
00:23:03,260 --> 00:23:05,260
C it is! We storm in from the second floor!

382
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:06,220
Alright!

383
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:15,760
Damn it! There must be other options!
Let me keep going!

384
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:36,140
Either way, today is the worst day ever,

385
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:40,540
so why is there no decent ending?

386
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:43,660
What is going on with today's story?

387
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:48,920
This is today's Kochikame flowchart.

388
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:53,440
There isn't a single decent punchline!

389
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:59,060
Damn it, I'm done with this terrible story!

390
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:01,060
The end, the end!

391
00:24:02,380 --> 00:24:04,200
Hehehehehehe

392
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:36,460
I wonder why Honda's personality
changes when he rides a bike.

393
00:24:36,460 --> 00:24:43,380
I wonder why Higurashi Neruo only
wakes up once every four years.

394
00:24:46,220 --> 00:24:52,540
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryo-san,

395
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:59,580
yet he lends out tanks and fighter jets so easily.
I wonder why.

396
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:06,900
Reiko is incredibly rich,

397
00:25:08,540 --> 00:25:12,460
yet she works at the police box.
I wonder why.

398
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:14,720
I wonder why.

399
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:15,940
I wonder why.

400
00:25:16,540 --> 00:25:17,200
Why?

401
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:17,920
Why?

402
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:18,600
Why?

403
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:19,540
I wonder why.

404
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:33,360
Chief Ohara is being
transferred to headquarters?

405
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:37,960
He was a noisy old man,
but it feels lonely to think he's gone.

406
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:43,600
Alright, let's all chip in and give the Chief
the Japanese sword he wanted as a farewell gift.

407
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:46,980
Make sure you get it right,
since this is the last present.

408
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:50,800
That's Kameari over there!

409
00:25:51,900 --> 00:25:54,420
Surely it's Kameari!

410
00:25:54,980 --> 00:25:59,140
Everyone, come on over to our town!

411
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:00,680
Thank you.

